  "description": [
    "287 pages : 26 cm",
    "This book includes over 300 recipes, as well as chapter introductions and sidebar anecdotes that provide glimpses into the history and personalities of the Fargo-Moorhead Symphony Orchestra. Many orchestra members, guest artists, patrons, and friends provide photos as a souvenir of the symphony in it's 75th year",
    "Includes indexes of recipes and recipe contributors",
    "\"In celebration of 75 years of music\"--T.p",
    "Article from the 1931 Fargo Forum \"1,000 applaud civic concert: Fargo Orchestra makes distinct musical history contribution / William Ballou. -- Letter from the President / Carlton Hunke, President Fargo Moorhead Symphony Orchestra Board of Trustees -- Mission statement from the FMSO -- Current Board of Trustees and Music DIrector -- Acknowledgements / Lyn Nichols -- THROUGH THE YEARS. The \"Thirties, Forties, Fifties, Sixties, and Seventies / Lois Vogel ; The \"Eigthies\" / Jane Ahlin ; The \"Nineties\" and \"A New Century\" / MaryAnn Berg. -- RECIPES. Appetizers and beverages ; Breakfast, muffins and eggs ; Pasta, rice and beans ; Poultry, game and meats ; Seafood, fish and shellfish ; Salads, soups and sides ; Cakes, cookies and desserts ; Lagniappe -- \"A tale of the tails\" / Bernard Rubenstein -- Conductors, past 75 years -- Orchestra: first and current -- Board members: past 75 years -- Concept: the color of music"
  ],
